===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|caecus|caecum|invisible, hidden}}, {{clipping|la|[[intestīnum]] [[caecus|caecum]]||blind gut|nocap=1|nocat=1}}, translation of {{der|en|grc|[[τυφλόν|τῠφλὸν]] [[ἔντερον]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsiː.kəm/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-caecum.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːkəm|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|caeca}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} A [[cavity]] open at one end (such as the [[blind#English: exitless|blind]] end of a [[duct]]), especially a blind [[pouch]] connected to the [[large intestine]] between the [[ileum]] and the [[colon]].
#: {{syn|en|blind gut}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1970|author=w:J. G. Ballard|title=w:The Atrocity Exhibition|passage=After a preliminary course in anatomy it was found that '''caecum''' and transverse colon also provided excellent sites for excitation.}}

